  "entry": "code/app.py",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Simulate how a crew's circadian clock drifts sol by sol on Mars (24.6167 h day), and from that compute a cognitive Performance Index, GREEN/YELLOW/RED alert levels and a 480 nm light-therapy prescription, for a chosen mission length, chronotype, wake time and phototherapy correction factor. Data used in the run: none. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
